cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt the Research Companion, please cite it."
title: "Research Companion: a verification-first research collaboration for AI coding agents"
authors:
  - family-names: "Liegertová"
    given-names: "Michaela"
version: 0.3.1
date-released: "2026-07-05"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A drop-in Claude Code configuration that turns an AI agent into a thoughtful
  research colleague designed to protect researchers against de-skilling: a
  six-phase lifecycle grounded in current literature, decisions signed in the
  researcher's own words and enforced by hooks, every specification run
  auto-logged, finished work verified blind by a fresh-eyes reviewer, and the
  researcher's calibration kept in training. Drafted with Claude (Fable 5) and
  rebuilt from a live, sealed-truth test arc; the materials practise the
  verification they preach.
